# Root build context. Used by the two services that build from `.`:
# prefect_worker (harvester/Dockerfile) and scheduler
# (download_scheduler/Dockerfile). Both need only the Python projects, the
# numbered SQL files and Obis_Datasets.json — everything else is transfer cost.
#
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore. A bare `node_modules` here
# matches ONLY a top-level entry, so anything meant to be excluded at any depth
# needs an explicit `**/` prefix. That is how 148 MB of
# harvester/ckan_harvester_cache stayed in the context while the root-level
# name was listed. Keep the two files in step in intent, not in syntax.

# --- Subtrees no root-context image needs -----------------------------------
# frontend/ (529 MB with node_modules) and web-api/ build from their OWN
# contexts; nginx and database likewise. test/ and docs/ ship in nothing.
frontend
web-api
nginx
test
docs
.github
.git
.vscode

# --- Virtualenvs and caches -------------------------------------------------
# `venv` alone never matched `.venv`, which is the name uv actually creates:
# four of them, 1.6 GB.
**/venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules

# --- Harvest / download artefacts -------------------------------------------
# harvester/ckan_harvester_cache alone is 148 MB; harvest-prod 96 MB. None of
# it is build input — the caches are re-fetched at run time into volumes.
**/harvester_cache
**/ckan_harvester_cache
**/harvester_logs
**/harvest
**/harvest-prod
**/downloads
**/cde_download*
# The harvest OUTPUT directory (harvest_obis()'s default folder="./obis/", so
# it lands beside the run's cwd: repo root, or harvester/ when run from there).
# ANCHORED deliberately. harvester/cde_harvester/sources/obis is a source
# package of the same name, and a bare `**/obis` matched it too: the worker
# image shipped without it, and `python -m cde_harvester` died on
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'cde_harvester.sources.obis'` before it
# could register its deployments, so every harvest failed.
#
# Do not reach for a `!` exception instead. `!harvester/**/*.csv` at the bottom
# of this file already makes BuildKit walk into excluded directories and judge
# each file on its own, and a directory pattern does not match the paths
# beneath it — which is why harvester/obis/*.csv reaches the context today even
# though harvester/obis is listed here. Another exception widens that hole.
/obis
harvester/obis
**/obis_cache
# ...but `**/obis` also matched harvester/cde_harvester/sources/obis, so the
# image shipped without the OBIS source package and every container died on
# `import cde_harvester.__main__` -> ModuleNotFoundError: cde_harvester.sources.obis.
# Re-include it explicitly (same idiom as the CSV rule at the bottom).
!harvester/cde_harvester/sources/obis
nginx/logs
nginx/logrotate_state

# --- Runtime config, never baked into an image ------------------------------
# The harvest config is supplied at run time on purpose (see harvester/Dockerfile).
harvest_config.yaml
harvest_config.production.yaml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# --- Secrets and local junk -------------------------------------------------
**/*.env
**/.env.*
.claude
**/.DS_Store
notforrepo
.vscode_
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/*.ipynb

# --- Build outputs and bulk data --------------------------------------------
**/dist
**/build
out
**/*.pdf
**/*.rdb
**/*.csv
!harvester/**/*.csv
